  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved policy enviroment and employment opportunities especially for youth and women in Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Identifying employment especially youth employment as a national priority is situated within the National Development Plan and the Renewed Hope Agenda of the current administration and the Nigerian Youth Employment Action Plan (NIYEAP) 2021 to 2024, which aims to contribute to the achievement of decent, productive, and freely chosen employment for young people, the Ilo developed a project that responds to implementing recommendations regarding employment governance frameworks contained in the NIYEAP and National Employment Policy (NEP). 

The intervention seeks to develop the capacities of Federal Ministry of Labour and Employment (FMLE), the National Employment Council (NEC), the Federal Ministry of Youth Development (FMYD) and the State Employment Councils (SEC) in the implementation of the revised National Employment Policy and for meaningful and sustainable youth engagement and decent work opportunities for Nigeria&#x2019;s youth population.</narrative>
  </description>
